From: Marionette AirDrop driver research
Subject: [EXPERIMENTAL] mlo: query disconnect flag without a sleeping lock

Observed on candidate 0052 during peer-unmap: ce_tasklet -> dp_tx_delete_flow_pool
-> policy_mgr_is_mlo_sta_disconnected -> qdf_mutex_acquire/release WARN.
LTO inlines wlan_vdev_mlme_is_mlo_vdev into that policy function.

Snapshot the aligned capability word for this read-only query. Preserve the
MLD presence check and all per-link CM state checks. Do not change structure
layout, lock types, refcounts, or the global MLO flag/accounting writer APIs.
The DP policy wrapper already owns WLAN_POLICY_MGR_ID on the queried vdev.
This is not a fix for the separate monitor DELETE-before-STOP warning.

--- a/qca-wifi-host-cmn/umac/mlo_mgr/src/wlan_mlo_mgr_sta.c
+++ b/qca-wifi-host-cmn/umac/mlo_mgr/src/wlan_mlo_mgr_sta.c
@@ -19,6 +19,7 @@
  * DOC: contains MLO manager STA related api's
  */
 
+#include <linux/compiler.h>
 #include <wlan_cmn.h>
 #include <wlan_mlo_mgr_sta.h>
 #include <wlan_cm_public_struct.h>
@@ -125,7 +126,17 @@
 	struct wlan_mlo_dev_context *mlo_dev_ctx = vdev->mlo_dev_ctx;
 	uint8_t i = 0;
 
-	if (!mlo_dev_ctx || !wlan_vdev_mlme_is_mlo_vdev(vdev))
+	/*
+	 * DP calls this query from the peer-unmap tasklet while holding a
+	 * referenced vdev. The public is_mlo_vdev accessor takes a mutex to
+	 * serialize flag updates with pdev MLO accounting, which cannot run
+	 * here. This query needs only the flag snapshot, not that accounting.
+	 * Its lock never protected the subsequent per-link CM state reads.
+	 * Keep the existing MLD/link-state decision; do not bypass live MLO.
+	 */
+	if (!mlo_dev_ctx ||
+	    !(READ_ONCE(vdev->vdev_mlme.vdev_feat_ext2_caps) &
+	      WLAN_VDEV_FEXT2_MLO))
 		return true;
 
 	for (i =  0; i < WLAN_UMAC_MLO_MAX_VDEVS; i++) {
